// array-sum-indexed.lmc - OPTIONAL EXTENSION, my own illustration (NOT from OCR).
// Self-modifying code: instructions are just numbers in memory, so a program can change itself.
// To walk along an array, the program rewrites its own first instruction
// (LDA data -> LDA data+1 -> ...) by adding 1 to the instruction word itself.
// Layout is hand-fixed: `data` is mailbox 15, so the first instruction is 515 (LDA 15)
// and `lastins` = 520 (LDA 20) marks "one past the end of the array".
// Output: 24  (4+7+1+9+3)
loop    LDA data        // mailbox 0 - this instruction gets modified each pass
        ADD total
        STA total
        LDA loop        // read the instruction word itself (e.g. 515)
        ADD one         // 516 = LDA 16, i.e. the next array element
        STA loop        // write it back over mailbox 0
        SUB lastins
        BRZ finished
        BRA loop
finished LDA total
        OUT
        HLT
total   DAT 0
one     DAT 1
lastins DAT 520
data    DAT 4
        DAT 7
        DAT 1
        DAT 9
        DAT 3
